target: skills/review/review-loop/plan.py
verify: bash skills/review/review-loop/plan.test.sh
expect: FAIL  an unreadable store is surfaced as the alarm being unavailable, not swallowed
why:    plan.py printed the alarm only when it exited 0 and said nothing otherwise, and an empty alarm is also what a healthy record prints. So the one state in which the alarm cannot look at the record at all — a store `looper stats` cannot read, its only non-zero exit — read exactly like "nothing is repeating", at the one moment the skill checks. Needs looper on PATH to run; without it the check skips and this entry survives rather than passing falsely.
--- old
    if rc != 0:
        # An empty alarm is also what a working alarm prints over a healthy record, so
--- new
    if False:
        # An empty alarm is also what a working alarm prints over a healthy record, so
